      "title": "Noun classes (class wheel)",
      "language_code": "sw",
      "steps": [
        {
          "kind": "learn",
          "duration_seconds": 22,
          "body_en": "Kiswahili groups nouns into classes shown by prefixes on singular and plural forms. LingAfriq Stage-1 concord checks only the §3.3 pairs m/wa and ki/vi (tools/content_engine/kits/sw/kit.yaml; DECISIONS P4-044). The see step uses a class wheel: spin to browse, or tap a segment when reduced motion is on (P7-933).",
